  "answer_text": "The XOps Network Playbook for SCIM Provisioning Failed lists three troubleshooting moves: 1) Inspect the audit and provisioning logs (e.g., in Azure Enterprise Applications > Cato Networks Provisioning) to determine if a configuration change or error triggered the failure. 2) Review the documented possible causes (credential mismatches, missing attributes, insufficient licenses, group/app scoping, etc.) to identify the likely root cause. 3) Make targeted changes by reassigning or removing users or groups in the IdP or CMA and then re-run provisioning. ",
